  "body": "https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#algorithm-declaration currently encourages algorithm definitions of the form\r\n\r\n> To [infinitive], given [parameters], perform the following steps. They return a [return type].\r\n\r\nHowever, call sites need to capture that return value, so they wind up looking like\r\n\r\n> Let [var] be the result of [gerunding], given [parameters].\r\n\r\nIn Bikeshed, that means the definition winds up looking like\r\n\r\n```html\r\nTo <dfn lt=\"infinitive|gerunding\">infinitive</dfn> ...\r\n```\r\n\r\nOr authors forget to include the `lt`, which forces callers to add it to every call site. https://github.com/whatwg/streams/pull/1079 has an example of fixing this forgetfulness.\r\n\r\nAlgorithm authors should instead write something like\r\n\r\n> [Gerunding], given [parameters], consists of the following steps, which return a [return type]:\r\n\r\nThis makes the call site look more like the definition and avoids the need for extra markup.",
